# Rust / Cargo
/target/
# Cargo.lock is deliberately COMMITTED. This is an application, not a library,
# and two things depend on a fixed dependency set: a release tag must rebuild
# into the same binary, and the seeded-RNG determinism the balance methodology
# rests on assumes `rand` does not drift underneath it (see the pin comment in
# Cargo.toml).

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Bevy
*.blend1

# Match logs (for debugging)
match_logs/
# egui_kittest transient snapshot artifacts (keep only the blessed *.png baseline)
tests/snapshots/*.new.png
tests/snapshots/*.old.png
tests/snapshots/*.diff.png
